MID_LGV_1_M09_Kai_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Kai_m01_001: So, imagine there's people who love each other.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Kai_m01_002: But they get split up because of their love.\nPretty lousy situation, huh?
MID_LGV_1_M09_Kai_m01_003: It's really tough being a grown-up.
MID_LGA_1_M09_Kai_m01: <BLN>Pretty lousy situation...
MID_LGV_1_M09_Bel_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Bel_m01_001: The chariot advances. To control the opponent's\nwar elephant, the high priest slinks to the side...
MID_LGV_1_M09_Bel_m01_002: Knowledge of a strategy game can help in\ncommanding allies.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Bel_m01_003: A mere game it may be, but one is reading their foe's\nmovements and adhering to the rules of battle.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Bel_m01_004: So it has value. Games I played in the past, I replay\nin my head as a thought exercise.
MID_LGA_1_M09_Bel_m01: <BLN>I know it's just a game.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Dit_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Dit_m01_001: I have been to see a play. It told the tale of some of\nthe strongest warriors in this land's history.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Dit_m01_002: The hero Arago, and the champion Breza. I wish I\ncould meet them.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Dit_m01_003: All I can do is imagine how they would fight.
MID_LGA_1_M09_Dit_m01: <BLN>If only I could meet them.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Tal_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Tal_m01_001: You've proven yourself in the tournament well\nenough. Perhaps I could ask your perspective...
MID_LGV_1_M09_Tal_m01_002: What if you were chasing a mystery, only to find that\nthe answers you're looking for could turn deadly?
MID_LGV_1_M09_Tal_m01_003: If the lives of your friends were on the line, what\nwould you do?
MID_LGV_1_M09_Tal_m01_004: <NCA>Tell him you'd pursue the mystery.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Tal_m01_005: <NCB>Tell him you wouldn't let comrades face danger.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Tal_m01_006: <ACA>Aha! So even with the risk of death, you'd still\npress on? Funny... I'd do the same.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Tal_m01_007: <ACB>Huh... Reasonable. But no fun at all.
MID_LGA_1_M09_Tal_m01: <BLN>Hey, can I ask you something?
MID_LGV_1_M09_Orh_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Orh_m01_001: Helping out with cleaning the temple and preparing\nrituals is a nice change of pace.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Orh_m01_002: I'm always delighted to be of help, and I'm getting\nbetter at minding my strength during tasks.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Orh_m01_003: What messes I've made, crushing things while\ncleaning them! Oh, the plates I've shattered!
MID_LGV_1_M09_Orh_m01_004: But I've become much more deft in doing such\ntasks without disaster. Years of experience!
MID_LGA_1_M09_Orh_m01: <BLN>A nice change of pace.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Seo_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Seo_m01_001: Bonaventure complained to me that the queen of\na nation should not roam about unattended.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Seo_m01_002: But it is not in my nature to disguise my majesty.\nA queen walks where she pleases with dignity.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Seo_m01_003: What have I to fear from a robber? I could strangle\nthem to death one-handed.
MID_LGA_1_M09_Seo_m01: <BLN>What have I to fear?
MID_LGV_1_M09_Led_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Led_m01_001: Winning the Heroic Games meant everything to me.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Led_m01_002: And now... I've lost. Heh.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Led_m01_003: It doesn't change what I have to do. Nothing will.
MID_LGA_1_M09_Led_m01: <BLN>Well, I lost.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Anh_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Anh_m01_001: A customer asked what Bagua is. I tried to explain,\nbut I'm not sure they understood what I was saying.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Anh_m01_002: It's easy to say my work is an ancient academic study\nof the laws of the heavens and earth.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Anh_m01_003: But true understanding requires training. Should I\nhave suggested that instead of trying to explain?
MID_LGA_1_M09_Anh_m01: <BLN>I'm not sure they understood.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Tia_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Tia_m01_001: I wonder if Fabio will invite me to play board games\nwith him again?
MID_LGV_1_M09_Tia_m01_002: He wasn't very familiar with Dagdan games, but he\npicked them up right away. He's good!
MID_LGA_1_M09_Tia_m01: <BLN>He's good!
MID_LGV_1_M09_Pet_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Pet_m01_001: Tialla seemed to enjoy playing board games\nwith Fabio.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Pet_m01_002: I wonder if Fabio would teach me how to play?
MID_LGV_1_M09_Pet_m01_003: I'd like to get good and surprise Tialla!
MID_LGA_1_M09_Pet_m01: <BLN>Maybe he'd teach me...
MID_LGV_1_M09_Hur_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Hur_m01_001: Lowtown has always been dangerous. Just the\nother day, I was attacked on my way home.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Hur_m01_002: But targeting a priest, and one trained by Centurio\nat that, was a major blunder.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Hur_m01_003: I knocked them over the head and apprehended\nthem on the spot. Aurora thought it was great!
MID_LGA_1_M09_Hur_m01: <BLN>Lowtown is dangerous...
MID_LGV_1_M09_Max_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Max_m01_001: Goliath and me are made out like villains, so most\npeople in the capital fear us.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Max_m01_002: But even if they heckle us from the stands, they can't\nmeet our eyes when we meet them.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Max_m01_003: Heh. Heh HEH! It's lonely when all you want to do is\nplay with them...
MID_LGV_1_M09_Max_m01_004: No one will even get near us. Though that can be a\nblessing too. Hah!
MID_LGA_1_M09_Max_m01: <BLN>It's a little lonely.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Gol_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Gol_m01_001: When I'm in the arena, I think about my old friends.\nLike this gladiator I used to go drinking with.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Gol_m01_002: REAL strong. But then he kicked the bucket out\nof nowhere.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Gol_m01_003: Right after telling me he'd buy me a drink too.\nWhy'd he have to go act like a fool?
MID_LGA_1_M09_Gol_m01: <BLN>I think about him sometimes.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Gat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Gat_m01_001: I thought it was impossible. The Demon Bear of\nBaphos is still alive?
MID_LGV_1_M09_Gat_m01_002: He was reputed to be a man who valued loyalty\nabove all else. How could he betray his lord?
MID_LGV_1_M09_Gat_m01_003: Did the Siege of Cydonia warp his values?\nOr maybe... Hm.
MID_LGA_1_M09_Gat_m01: <BLN>He's still alive.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Dan_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Dan_m01_001: Some call playwriting an easy job. "Oh, you just sit at\na desk and scratch at your paper." Hmph!
MID_LGV_1_M09_Dan_m01_002: The effort it takes to find the perfect words and\nweave them together with structure and artistry...
MID_LGV_1_M09_Dan_m01_003: Not to mention the research. The time a playwright\nmust take to see reality from all its angles!
MID_LGV_1_M09_Dan_m01_004: Yet somehow, a master auteur such as I can juggle\nbattle on one hand and writing on the other.
MID_LGA_1_M09_Dan_m01: <BLN>Abject ignorance!
MID_LGV_1_M09_Fab_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Fab_m01_001: I have had the chance to face off against Tialla in a\ngame many times now. As expected, she is skilled.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Fab_m01_002: It is comical, however, how determined she is to best\nme. It does endear her to me, I will admit.
MID_LGA_1_M09_Fab_m01: <BLN>A good time was had.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Esm_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Esm_m01_001: These eyes of mine are a treasure I got from my\nparents. I really like them.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Esm_m01_002: Just the other day, I took a peek in a jeweler's, and I\ngot a compliment too! As pretty as gems, they said.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Esm_m01_003: They gave me a discount because the jewelry suited\nme. I'll go help out at the store to return the kindness.
MID_LGA_1_M09_Esm_m01: <BLN>These eyes are a treasure.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Urs_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Urs_m01_001: I used to hate crowds, social events, and even\nday-to-day conversation...
MID_LGV_1_M09_Urs_m01_002: But thanks to Talimun, I don't mind them so\nmuch anymore.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Urs_m01_003: "Being visible can be an advantage, Ursula. You can't\nreally see others if you don't reveal yourself, after all."
MID_LGV_1_M09_Urs_m01_004: To this day, I still think he was referring to business.\nNevertheless... Words to live by.
MID_LGA_1_M09_Urs_m01: <BLN>It's all thanks to Talimun.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Sim_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Sim_m01_001: Might surprise you, but I like to carve little wooden\nstatues in my free time.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Sim_m01_002: Confused the hell out of Ludia the first time she\nsaw me doing it.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Sim_m01_003: I may love to fight, but there's plenty more to me\nthan just that.
MID_LGA_1_M09_Sim_m01: <BLN>Is it THAT surprising?
MID_LGV_1_M09_Lou_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Lou_m01_001: I like working for Talimun, but sometimes his\nrequests can feel pretty outrageous!
MID_LGV_1_M09_Lou_m01_002: But that's what makes Ursula so pivotal! It always\nseems like she knows exactly what he needs.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Lou_m01_003: Even in the few moments she's been caught\noff guard, she doesn't let it faze her one bit.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Lou_m01_004: If I'm going to be the next great merchant, I have to\nlearn all I can from her!
MID_LGA_1_M09_Lou_m01: <BLN>She's so impressive!
MID_LGV_1_M09_Fia_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Fia_m01_001: I still remember the cleric who tended to my wound...
MID_LGV_1_M09_Fia_m01_002: She saw my talents as a healer and agreed to train\nme as her student.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Fia_m01_003: Her life was modest, to be sure, but in modesty, she\nfound ways to live life to the fullest.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Fia_m01_004: Her final lesson was that...some wounds are beyond\nour mending. And in those deaths, we should pray...
MID_LGA_1_M09_Fia_m01: <BLN>I still remember her well...
MID_LGV_1_M09_Die_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Die_m01_001: Seriously...some of our opponents in the Heroic\nGames are pretty strange.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Die_m01_002: I thought I was used to all sorts of unusual folks,\ngiven my time with Orchel and Credna.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Die_m01_003: The world is far bigger than I thought. I guess\neverything in life is good experience.
MID_LGA_1_M09_Die_m01: <BLN>It's all good experience.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Lor_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Lor_m01_001: That Diego... He keeps telling me to be more\ncareful! To pay attention to this or that!
MID_LGV_1_M09_Lor_m01_002: And not just about my temple work. He comments\non everything I do.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Lor_m01_003: He doesn't have to tell me that stuff all the time!\nI hate being treated like a kid.
MID_LGA_1_M09_Lor_m01: <BLN>That Diego...
MID_LGV_1_M09_Set_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Set_m01_001: Hmm... It's you, I see. Could I trouble you for\nsome advice?
MID_LGV_1_M09_Set_m01_002: People have informed me on occasion that I can\nbe "difficult" or "stubborn."
MID_LGV_1_M09_Set_m01_003: I never intend to come across that way, however.\nSo, I'd like to know what I can do about this.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Set_m01_004: <NCA>Tell him this is exactly why he's difficult.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Set_m01_005: <NCB>Say it's part of his charm.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Set_m01_006: <ACA>What? But I'm simply stating my own issue and\ntaking an active hand in its resolution!
MID_LGV_1_M09_Set_m01_007: <ACA>But...are you saying it's my approach that's really the\nproblem? How perplexing! It's so natural for me!
MID_LGV_1_M09_Set_m01_008: <ACB>I appreciate that you think so. But that won't help\nme solve what troubles me with others.
MID_LGA_1_M09_Set_m01: <BLN>What should I do?
MID_LGV_1_M09_Nin_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Nin_m01_001: Yes, yes... All of you, thank you...
MID_LGV_1_M09_Nin_m01_002: This land's spirit magic... It draws upon the power\nof all you spirits who dwell here.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Nin_m01_003: Without you, no one would be able to wield such\nmagic... Yet they have no idea...
MID_LGA_1_M09_Nin_m01: <BLN>Thank you... All of you...
MID_LGV_1_M09_Bon_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Bon_m01_001: Hmm. It seems we will soon have time on our hands.\nPerhaps I should dabble in cooking.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Bon_m01_002: I shall study every step, from procuring ingredients\nto technique in the kitchen, before I begin in earnest.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Bon_m01_003: A recipe is like a battlefield stratagem. One can lose\noneself in preparing to execute it.
MID_LGA_1_M09_Bon_m01: <BLN>An enjoyable pastime...
MID_LGV_1_M09_Tob_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Tob_m01_001: The people of the empire turn their backs on us just\n'cause we're from Saramis.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Tob_m01_002: And the kids here think I'm scary. It really gets me\ndown when I look at 'em and they start to cry.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Tob_m01_003: Is there any way I can do somethin' to help folks\nhere think better of Saramis?
MID_LGV_1_M09_Tob_m01_004: <NCA>Suggest smiling more.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Tob_m01_005: <NCB>Suggest dining with them.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Tob_m01_006: <ACA>Oh, good idea! Smilin' is a great first step.\nBaw haw haw haw!
MID_LGV_1_M09_Tob_m01_007: <ACB>Hey, yeah! A little ale puts anyone in a good mood.\nOh, but the kids can't drink, huh.
MID_LGA_1_M09_Tob_m01: <BLN>How can I get 'em to like us?
MID_LGV_1_M09_Lil_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Lil_m01_001: Heh heh. It's almost time to take my recent earnings\nto a jeweler.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Lil_m01_002: But I can't rest easy yet. Not until I'm sure I didn't\nget tricked into buying any fake gems.
MID_LGA_1_M09_Lil_m01: <BLN>Gotta convert all this cash.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Lys_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Lys_m01_001: I always learn a thing or two about trends from my\ndinners with the local women.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Lys_m01_002: It's both a good time and a chance to polish my\nconversational skills. Now who should I ask out next?
MID_LGA_1_M09_Lys_m01: <BLN>I always learn a thing or two.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Buc_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Buc_m01_001: In truth...I am glad it worked out as it has.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Buc_m01_002: Her path has not been without its obstacles. I should\nprobably have stopped her sooner.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Buc_m01_003: But now that she's eliminated from the Heroic\nGames, she can't carry out her plan.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Buc_m01_004: If she still insists on finding a way...then I'll just have\nto stop her. Even if it costs me my role as her guard.
MID_LGA_1_M09_Buc_m01: <BLN>I'm glad, frankly.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Sci_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Sci_m01_001: There's a troupe called Nasshim's Circus that has\nsome marvelous performers in its ranks.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Sci_m01_002: Yet I've heard next to nothing of them lately. Given\ntheir skill, I'd expect more talk of their location.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Sci_m01_003: Travel has its dangers, of course. I'll pray to Kalla for\nthe group's safety.
MID_LGA_1_M09_Sci_m01: <BLN>A particular circus...
MID_LGV_1_M09_Moo_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Moo_m01_001: The Heroic Games' rules let people get immediate\nassistance—extra fighters, medical treatment.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Moo_m01_002: I was walking out of the arena and I passed someone\nrunning toward the colosseum with a big bag.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Moo_m01_003: I thought that was so cool. Like, your day job is\nsaving people?
MID_LGV_1_M09_Moo_m01_004: <NCA>Express your admiration for doctors.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Moo_m01_005: <NCB>Ask if Mu admires doctors.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Moo_m01_006: <ACA>Y-yeah, true! I mean, how can you not admire them,\nin this line of work? It's dangerous!
MID_LGV_1_M09_Moo_m01_007: <ACA>Y-yeah, true! I mean, how can you not admire them,\nin this line of work? It's dangerous!
MID_LGV_1_M09_Moo_m01_008: <ACB>Yeah! Someday I wanna be like them too.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Moo_m01_009: <ACB>Yeah! Someday I wanna be like them too.
MID_LGA_1_M09_Moo_m01: <BLN>It was amazing...
MID_LGV_1_M09_Mic_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Mic_m01_001: When there's a good deal on provisions, I tend to buy\na lot.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Mic_m01_002: I guess it's alright. If I cook, someone'll eat it, as I\nalways say.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Mic_m01_003: I just wish Mu would come and join in. Oh, well.\nComplaining about that doesn't do any good.
MID_LGA_1_M09_Mic_m01: <BLN>I ended up buying too much!
MID_LGV_1_M09_Oly_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Oly_m01_001: Life is a protracted string of bad experiences.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Oly_m01_002: But these are intertwined with good experiences\nas well.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Oly_m01_003: So, as you feel despair, try to feel hope. As you hope,\nremember your sorrows. This is the key to strength.
MID_LGA_1_M09_Oly_m01: <BLN>As long as one is alive.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Naz_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Naz_m01_001: I've been talking with the folks at the training\ngrounds to find out how their matches went...
MID_LGV_1_M09_Naz_m01_002: They showed me their training methods, and I taught\nthem how to release their inner power explosively.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Naz_m01_003: Oh no! Was that something I'm supposed to\nkeep secret?
MID_LGV_1_M09_Naz_m01_004: Well, nobody seemed like they really understood all\nthe talk of energy flow, so maybe it's fine?
MID_LGA_1_M09_Naz_m01: <BLN>Folks at the training grounds...
MID_LGV_1_M09_Sar_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Sar_m01_001: Jiang is such a good girl. Even though she is just a\nchild, she can be relied upon to do her job well.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Sar_m01_002: I used to help my mother when I was little too.\nIt was hard work, but those were good times.
MID_LGA_1_M09_Sar_m01: <BLN>Jiang is a good girl.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Dai_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Dai_m01_001: I think Anatolia is taking on too much.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Dai_m01_002: So, you know, be nice to her if you see her. Yeah?
MID_LGV_1_M09_Dai_m01_003: My woman's strong, so I'm not really worried. But\nI bet it'll help her to have people to talk to.
MID_LGA_1_M09_Dai_m01: <BLN>Anatolia...
MID_LGV_1_M09_Hal_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Hal_m01_001: Oh no! I've lost all my street-performance gear\nsomewhere. I've gotta do something!
MID_LGV_1_M09_Hal_m01_002: I promised I'd perform tricks for some children...
MID_LGV_1_M09_Hal_m01_003: What do I do? I guess I should get searching, maybe?
MID_LGV_1_M09_Hal_m01_004: <NCA>Suggest she ask soldiers at the temples.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Hal_m01_005: <NCB>Suggest she perform tricks without equipment.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Hal_m01_006: <ACA>Y-you're right but... Ugh, I've got such bad memories\nof temple soldiers.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Hal_m01_007: <ACA>Y-you're right but... Ugh, I've got such bad memories\nof temple soldiers.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Hal_m01_008: <ACB>Ha! Nasshim said the same thing! A-alright!\nI'm going to start practicing and do my best!
MID_LGV_1_M09_Hal_m01_009: <ACB>Ha! Nasshim said the same thing! A-alright!\nI'll start practicing and give it my all!
MID_LGA_1_M09_Hal_m01: <BLN>I should start searching? Maybe?
MID_LGV_1_M09_Guj_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Guj_m01_001: There was a time when I lived and died for the\nsmoked meat made by the Har Hali. Delicious stuff!
MID_LGV_1_M09_Guj_m01_002: It pairs well with a mug of suds too, so I used to\ntake jobs with them to get a meaty reward.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Guj_m01_003: One day they invited me to a party...and I nearly\nwound up as one of their sacrifices. Tight spot!
MID_LGA_1_M09_Guj_m01: <BLN>A tight spot for sure!
MID_LGV_1_M09_Yan_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Yan_m01_001: It's said that the truly stalwart are like wooden\ndummies—no passion stirring one's form.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Yan_m01_002: Aspiring to be such a wooden dummy, I sat\nlakeside and meditated. But, beauty abounded!
MID_LGV_1_M09_Yan_m01_003: I found myself wanting to toast nature with a\ndrink! So much for a life unstirred by passion.
MID_LGA_1_M09_Yan_m01: <BLN>A difficult feat.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Iio_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Iio_m01_001: I shared a meal with Catania a ways back. She\ncalled herself...a knight of the highest quality.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Iio_m01_002: She should be proud of herself—the way she trains\nevery day. Her ability is exceptional.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Iio_m01_003: But her pride verges on conceit, I think? It's not\nsomething I could understand, at least.
MID_LGA_1_M09_Iio_m01: <BLN>Why does she act that way?
MID_LGV_1_M09_Pep_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Pep_m01_001: We ourselves can barely contain our elation, now\nthat the Heroic Games have entered their late phase!
MID_LGV_1_M09_Pep_m01_002: It must be nearly time for the grand announcement\nthat opens the next match!
MID_LGV_1_M09_Pep_m01_003: We must throw laurels in your direction for showing\nus such remarkable battles in the games.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Pep_m01_004: Though we lost our friendly match, we did make\nour kingdom well-known to this empire.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Pep_m01_005: May the lands of Brigid and Dagda henceforth\nbe joined in harmony!
MID_LGA_1_M09_Pep_m01: <BLN>We are truly excited!
MID_LGV_1_M09_Noc_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Noc_m01_001: I really upset some soldiers from Saramis. But I'm\nnot sure why!
MID_LGV_1_M09_Noc_m01_002: Isn't "Her Shiny Goldness" respectful enough when\nspeaking about their queen?
MID_LGV_1_M09_Noc_m01_003: What better way to praise someone who's tough and\nglittery? I even did the whole royal "Her" part!
MID_LGA_1_M09_Noc_m01: <BLN>How'd I offend them?
MID_LGV_1_M09_Sop_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Sop_m01_001: That restaurant I went to... The food was so tasty\nthat I can't stop thinking about it...
MID_LGV_1_M09_Sop_m01_002: I must let all the other priests know about it.\nThey're so busy. They deserve deliciousness!
MID_LGV_1_M09_Sop_m01_003: It'd make me even happier if we could just plunge\ninto a tasty meal together. I wonder if they would?
MID_LGA_1_M09_Sop_m01: <BLN>I need to share this!
MID_LGV_1_M09_Cat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Cat_m01_001: I was dining with Io recently, but I found myself\nstartled by his high ideals.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Cat_m01_002: I can't fault his ambition and effort—not at all. But\nhe seems to struggle with the practicals of life.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Cat_m01_003: It's a shame, because I can't help but notice his\nsuperb appearance and capabilities. Ah, youth...
MID_LGA_1_M09_Cat_m01: <BLN>Perhaps it's his youth.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Ned_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Ned_m01_001: I imagine that a lot of people have traveled far\nand wide to participate in the Heroic Games.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Ned_m01_002: I love a good journey myself. I roamed widely after\nleaving my country until I settled down here.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Ned_m01_003: Wherever I traveled, I would challenge every\nwarrior to spar with me. Such memories!
MID_LGA_1_M09_Ned_m01: <BLN>Such memories!
MID_LGV_1_M09_Zac_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Zac_m01_001: The fighters who got this far in the games... They're\nkinda different from the earlier ones.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Zac_m01_002: Friggin' scary if you ask me. I don't want any\npiece of 'em.
MID_LGA_1_M09_Zac_m01: <BLN>Friggin' scary...
MID_LGV_1_M09_Maj_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Maj_m01_001: {SetColor=Gray}That idiot Dietrich... Gettin' on his high horse just\n'cause he's pretty and can swing a sword...{SetColor=Default}
MID_LGV_1_M09_Maj_m01_002: {SetColor=Gray}He only got into the damn games because of\nthe great Majide... Bah...{SetColor=Default}
MID_LGA_1_M09_Maj_m01: <BLN>That big idiot...
MID_LGV_1_M09_Ven_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Ven_m01_001: Years ago, it was all weddings and babies being born.\nLife all around...
MID_LGV_1_M09_Ven_m01_002: Now when I look up old comrades, I find nothing\nbut poor health and funerals.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Ven_m01_003: None of them are up and at 'em like me, chasing\ntheir dreams! Pathetic, really.
MID_LGA_1_M09_Ven_m01: <BLN>I'm a lifelong example!
MID_LGV_1_M09_Ini_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Ini_m01_001: I used to make friends easily when I trained with a\nbow and arrow. But that was when I was young.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Ini_m01_002: These days I don't make many friends with\nmy bow.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Ini_m01_003: I wish I had more friends at this age...
MID_LGA_1_M09_Ini_m01: <BLN>Making friends...
MID_LGV_1_M09_Jas_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Jas_m01_001: I'm looking forward to more matches so much.\nI can't help smiling!
MID_LGV_1_M09_Jas_m01_002: The remaining contenders are sure to make for\nan absolute storm of great fighting.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Jas_m01_003: I might not be the youngest warrior around here,\nbut I still get excited as ever!
MID_LGA_1_M09_Jas_m01: <BLN>More matches!
MID_LGV_1_M09_Ale_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Ale_m01_001: When I walk around the city, lots of people\napproach me with kind things to say. Why is that?
MID_LGV_1_M09_Ale_m01_002: I often approach people whom I sense need help.\nBut I...don't particularly need any myself.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Ale_m01_003: Do I look like I'm lost or something? Because\nthat'd just be plain embarrassing.
MID_LGA_1_M09_Ale_m01: <BLN>Why do they do that?
MID_LGV_1_M09_Cen_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Cen_m01_001: I'm certain there's some evil scheme in motion\nalongside the Heroic Games.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Cen_m01_002: Nobody else has spotted it yet, but I'm keeping a\nwatchful eye now more than ever... 
MID_LGV_1_M09_Cen_m01_003: I'm making it clear to my people that now, more than\never, we must focus on security in Dagsion.
MID_LGA_1_M09_Cen_m01: <BLN>We must focus...
MID_LGV_1_M09_Kir_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Kir_m01_001: Urrggh. So tired... My dreams are plagued by\nthe ghosts of guys I've sent to their deaths...
MID_LGV_1_M09_Kir_m01_002: W-wait! Is THAT a ghost?! Uh, never mind.\nJ-just a joke...
MID_LGV_1_M09_Kir_m01_003: Wh-what is going on... I'm losing it...
MID_LGA_1_M09_Kir_m01: <BLN>So tired...
MID_LGV_1_M09_Nuz_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Nuz_m01_001: There is often an ominous quality to the battles of\nthe Heroic Games.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Nuz_m01_002: Like when Bahr Vahn appeared with his new\nleft hand...
MID_LGV_1_M09_Nuz_m01_003: I hope nothing so gruesome happens again.
MID_LGA_1_M09_Nuz_m01: <BLN>These battles can be ominous.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Gab_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Gab_m01_001: Some in my line of work say it's fine if all you feed\nyour gladiators is bakul. Pah!
MID_LGV_1_M09_Gab_m01_002: Bein' healthy means eating food from all over the\nland and sea. Not just grains.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Gab_m01_003: Those poor gladiators could lose their lives any day.\nThe least they deserve's a good meal.
MID_LGA_1_M09_Gab_m01: <BLN>I want them eating well.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Lin_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Lin_m01_001: Do you know what's been shut away under here?
MID_LGV_1_M09_Lin_m01_002: The bowels of Dagsion. Through them have passed\ntens of thousands of lives.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Lin_m01_003: They're hidden, enormous, and unspeakable.
MID_LGA_1_M09_Lin_m01: <BLN>Do you know where we are?
MID_LGV_1_M09_Nat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Nat_m01_001: Did Queen Aswan know Bertrand was alive?
MID_LGV_1_M09_Nat_m01_002: Could that be why she accompanied us to Dagsion?
MID_LGA_1_M09_Nat_m01: <BLN>Could that be why?
MID_LGV_1_M09_Hri_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Hri_m01_001: This is my first day off in ages. It's nice to forget\nabout work and just stroll around the city.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Hri_m01_002: Especially one as vast as this. You could spend your\nwhole life here and not run out of new things to see.
MID_LGA_1_M09_Hri_m01: <BLN>I haven't had a day off in ages.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Ann_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Ann_m01_001: I had a chance encounter that got me interested\nin commerce.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Ann_m01_002: So I decided I'd try selling off some stuff I'd\nbought wholesale.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Ann_m01_003: After all, with the field narrowed down in the Heroic\nGames, there's less administrative work for me.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Ann_m01_004: But keep my little side venture a secret from the\ntemples, if you please!
MID_LGA_1_M09_Ann_m01: <BLN>I'm going to get into commerce!
MID_LGV_1_M09_Ann_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_Ann_m02_001: Something came up recently that piqued my interest\nin commerce.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Ann_m02_002: So I've been running a secret shop open only at night.
MID_LGV_1_M09_Ann_m02_003: I've got some pretty good stuff for sale! You should\ncome by after sundown and have a look.
MID_LGA_1_M09_Ann_m02: <BLN>Gotta keep this quiet...
MID_LGV_1_M09_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_B01_m01_001: I've got to sell, sell, sell while I can! When the Heroic\nGames end, there won't be as many customers.
MID_LGV_1_M09_B01_m01_002: I'm going to rake in the cash now so I can live the\ngood life for a while after.
MID_LGA_1_M09_B01_m01: <BLN>Gotta earn while I can!
MID_LGV_1_M09_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_B02_m01_001: My kusarik-hide gloves got torn. It's dangerous to\nuse the forge without them.
MID_LGV_1_M09_B02_m01_002: I need them repaired as soon as I can, but what am\nI going to do until they're ready?
MID_LGV_1_M09_B02_m01_003: I'd hate to have to borrow the boss's sweaty gloves\nagain. Ick.
MID_LGA_1_M09_B02_m01: <BLN>Ughhh...
MID_LGV_1_M09_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_B03_m01_001: Damn! I lost. But since I'm here, I may as well watch\nthe finals.
MID_LGV_1_M09_B03_m01_002: Maybe I'll get to see someone give the clan who\nbeat me a good thrashing!
MID_LGA_1_M09_B03_m01: <BLN>I lost!
MID_LGV_1_M09_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_B04_m01_001: The Lady of Lilies always carries a unique stuffed\ntoy with her.
MID_LGV_1_M09_B04_m01_002: Is that the fashion among noble ladies? I wonder if I\nought to buy one for my granddaughter.
MID_LGA_1_M09_B04_m01: <BLN>Where are they sold?
MID_LGV_1_M09_B05_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_B05_m01_001: The elephants were so big! I want to ride one. Ooh,\nI could raise one at home!
MID_LGV_1_M09_B05_m01_002: I want a pegasus too, and an ornius and an\natlas bear! Maybe if I beg Grandpa...
MID_LGA_1_M09_B05_m01: <BLN>I'd love it so much!
MID_LGV_1_M09_B06_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_B06_m01_001: The prophecies of Jehoshaphat are popular with the\npeople now. The archpriest doesn't see any issue.
MID_LGV_1_M09_B06_m01_002: Personally, I'd like to nip it in the bud. All this talk of\nthe end times only fosters a sense of panic.
MID_LGV_1_M09_B06_m01_003: Isn't it all a distorted reflection of the Ostoro's\nresentment at Bloodaxe Hanno defeating them?
MID_LGA_1_M09_B06_m01: <BLN>Can we allow this to continue?
MID_LGV_1_M09_B07_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_B07_m01_001: I admire Father Nomved of Credna's temple.\nHe's quiet and contemplative.
MID_LGV_1_M09_B07_m01_002: Credna also trusts him deeply. I hope I can build\nthat sort of relationship with a god someday.
MID_LGA_1_M09_B07_m01: <BLN>I admire him.
MID_LGV_1_M09_B08_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_B08_m01_001: Lord Solel the Sunbearer and Yu Phas, Keeper of\nDeath and Night, bore Aurora, Navigator's Clarion.
MID_LGV_1_M09_B08_m01_002: All of them are deities associated with the sky.\nI think of them whenever I look to the heavens.
MID_LGA_1_M09_B08_m01: <BLN>The deities of the sky...
MID_LGV_1_M09_B09_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_B09_m01_001: Oof... I told my old man not to drink so much booze,\nbut he doesn't listen.
MID_LGV_1_M09_B09_m01_002: He's a clumsy drunk, so he's constantly running into\nme. It gets on my nerves.
MID_LGA_1_M09_B09_m01: <BLN>Oof...
MID_LGV_1_M09_B10_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_B10_m01_001: I hate this! The inn I'm staying at raised their rates\njust because the Heroic Games are in full swing.
MID_LGV_1_M09_B10_m01_002: Well, they're not getting my business anymore—\nnot after gouging their customers like this.
MID_LGA_1_M09_B10_m01: <BLN>Never again!
MID_LGV_1_M09_B11_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_B11_m01_001: Lately, it's been a struggle to see what my hands are\ndoing when I'm cooking.
MID_LGV_1_M09_B11_m01_002: So my husband gave me some spectacles, with such\na cute design it made me blush!
MID_LGA_1_M09_B11_m01: <BLN>I'm not as young as I used to be...
MID_LGV_1_M09_B12_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_B12_m01_001: Most of the competitors who got knocked out in the\nqualifiers are still hanging around...but why?
MID_LGV_1_M09_B12_m01_002: Losers should pack up and go home. They're only\na nuisance around here.
MID_LGA_1_M09_B12_m01: <BLN>What a bunch of eyesores.
MID_LGV_1_M09_B13_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_B13_m01_001: You can ride a jamel across the desert, but is there\nan animal you can ride across the sea?
MID_LGV_1_M09_B13_m01_002: Some horses have wings, so I don't think it'd be\nweird for an ox to have fins.
MID_LGA_1_M09_B13_m01: <BLN>Is there such a thing?
MID_LGV_1_M09_B14_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_B14_m01_001: The Vandahl Trading Company has a broad network,\nbut that comes with a lot of resentment.
MID_LGV_1_M09_B14_m01_002: Their employees know it too, so they all have a bit\nof combat training. It's a tough line of work!
MID_LGA_1_M09_B14_m01: <BLN>The Vandahl Trading Company...
MID_LGV_1_M09_B15_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_B15_m01_001: The land of Dagda is warm, for the most part.\nBut I'd love to visit a cold country someday.
MID_LGV_1_M09_B15_m01_002: Maybe not freezing cold, but one where food doesn't\nspoil in the heat so quickly.
MID_LGA_1_M09_B15_m01: <BLN>I'd love to visit a cold climate.
MID_LGV_1_M09_B16_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_B16_m01_001: I've been sailing the Danann Sea for 20 years,\nbut the sailors of the Lir Sea are still beyond me.
MID_LGV_1_M09_B16_m01_002: The flow of the currents there is difficult to read. I\ntried them when I was young, but couldn't keep up.
MID_LGA_1_M09_B16_m01: <BLN>Those sailors of the Lir Sea...
MID_LGV_1_M09_B17_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_B17_m01_001: I saw a lovely person at the Saramis guesthouse\nand sent her an invitation to an evening soiree.
MID_LGV_1_M09_B17_m01_002: But she didn't show up. Oh, the sting of rejection...
MID_LGA_1_M09_B17_m01: <BLN>Did she even read it?
MID_LGV_1_M09_B18_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_B18_m01_001: Why does the Arago guesthouse have to be so close\nto ours?
MID_LGV_1_M09_B18_m01_002: Even after we've been here this long, I just can't\nseem to get along with the Arago crowd.
MID_LGV_1_M09_B18_m01_003: Especially their queen! She's a descendant of Arago,\nright? I don't want to deal with any of Dagda's blood.
MID_LGA_1_M09_B18_m01: <BLN>Why so close?
MID_LGV_1_M09_B19_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_B19_m01_001: I tried tenebato because I heard it's good for the\nskin, and it's actually tasty!
MID_LGV_1_M09_B19_m01_002: Enough so that I could eat it every day. If it makes\nme beautiful as well, then all the better!
MID_LGA_1_M09_B19_m01: <BLN>It's even better than I'd thought.
MID_LGV_1_M09_B20_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_B20_m01_001: Maybe Aurora actually died a long time ago...
MID_LGV_1_M09_B20_m01_002: She hasn't been seen for years, right? If you assume\nthat's true, everything starts to make sense.
MID_LGA_1_M09_B20_m01: <BLN>It's a terrible thought, but...
MID_LGV_1_M09_B21_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_B21_m01_001: The Vandahl Trading Company repaired the great\nlighthouse that had been left derelict for so long.
MID_LGV_1_M09_B21_m01_002: All the sailors are thrilled that their voyages have\nbecome that much easier now.
MID_LGA_1_M09_B21_m01: <BLN>Well done, Vandahl.
MID_LGV_1_M09_B22_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_B22_m01_001: That Anatolia has a sort of mystical aura that is\nhard to describe.
MID_LGV_1_M09_B22_m01_002: If you told me she was the Herald of the Pale Raven,\nI'd probably believe you.
MID_LGV_1_M09_B22_m01_003: 
MID_LGA_1_M09_B22_m01: <BLN>That Anatolia...
MID_LGV_1_M09_B23_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_B23_m01_001: Folks strung out on flamma get all fuzzy and start\nsaying stuff that makes no sense.
MID_LGV_1_M09_B23_m01_002: But they're not just babbling random words.
MID_LGV_1_M09_B23_m01_003: They'll talk about a city they've never been to, or\nsome person they couldn't possibly have met.
MID_LGA_1_M09_B23_m01: <BLN>It's strange.
MID_LGV_1_M09_B24_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_B24_m01_001: The seasoning known as garum that they use in this\nregion is thick, cloudy, and wonderfully aromatic.
MID_LGV_1_M09_B24_m01_002: Could fermented salted fish be the key? It's unusual,\nbut the flavor is rich and intriguing.
MID_LGV_1_M09_B24_m01_003: If one could find a way to neutralize the smell,\nit might be popular even in Fódlan.
MID_LGA_1_M09_B24_m01: <BLN>Is there profit potential here?
MID_LGV_1_M09_B25_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_B25_m01_001: There seem to be quite a few children born from\ngods and their human lovers.
MID_LGV_1_M09_B25_m01_002: The genealogies of these demigods are scattered\nthroughout Dagda as strong bloodlines.
MID_LGV_1_M09_B25_m01_003: Houses recognized as such receive support from the\ntemples and even some special privileges.
MID_LGV_1_M09_B25_m01_004: There are many in this land who'll do anything they\ncan to curry favor with these families.
MID_LGA_1_M09_B25_m01: <BLN>There are many demigods...
MID_LGV_1_M09_B26_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_B26_m01_001: Some parts of Dagsion are the kinds of places that\npeople who walk in broad daylight should never go.
MID_LGV_1_M09_B26_m01_002: This is one of them. If you catch my drift, you won't\ncome around here again.
MID_LGA_1_M09_B26_m01: <BLN>There's nothing to see here.
MID_LGV_1_M09_B27_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M09_B27_m01_001: There's no end to the couples who come to visit\nDagda's temple without a proper reason.
MID_LGV_1_M09_B27_m01_002: I don't know why they insist on it, but it's rather\nindecent of them to encroach on sacred ground!
MID_LGA_1_M09_B27_m01: <BLN>How indecent!